<title>AUSTRALIA: SOCCER-SOLOMON ISLANDS BEAT TAHITI 4-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SOLOMON ISLANDS BEAT TAHITI 4-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Solomon Islands beat Tahiti 4-1</p>
<p>(halftime 2-0) in an Oceania group one World Cup qualifying</p>
<p>match at Gabbie Stadium on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Solomon Islands - Robert Seni 38, Noel Berry 40, 81, Moses</p>
<p>Toata 90.</p>
<p>Tahiti - Jean Ludivion 84.</p>
<p>    Standings	   P   W   D   L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> Australia		2   2   0   0  18   0    6</p>
<p> Solomon Islands	2   1   0   1   4  14    3</p>
<p> Tahiti		   2   0   0   2   1   9    0</p>
<p>Next match: June 17, in Sydney, Australia v Solomon Islands.</p>
</text>
